__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Derived engine copy for self-contained distributions. The repository is the
# authority; this is staged at build time by
# receiver_reliance/generate_engine_manifest.py --stage and governed by
# receiver_reliance/engine_manifest.json, so it is never committed.
receiver_reliance/_engine/
# setuptools build residue. Written into the source tree by a wheel build; it is
# not part of the artifact and its presence breaks verify_hygiene, which reads
# `git diff --check` over tracked files.
*.egg-info/
# The same class, and both were missed once. build/ was committed by 72efd11,
# which put a second copy of the staged engine under version control and
# falsified the claim that the staged copy is never committed: a wheel could then
# be built from a clean clone without --stage, and tampering with only the
# committed copy produced a manifest-violating wheel while --check still exited 0
# (the import gate did catch it). dist/ is where the documented wheel build
# writes, so leaving it untracked-but-not-ignored made the charter gate fail for
# anyone who followed the distribution steps: the gate requires a clean tree
# including untracked files.
build/
dist/
